# Vercel frontend → HF Space (Gradio queue) or local FastAPI
# Local dev: VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000 (Vite proxy /api → localhost:8000 via vite.config.ts)
#   empty/localhost base → FastAPI transport (FormData POST /api/query)
# Production (Vercel): VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://YOUR_HF_USERNAME-satquery-backend.hf.space
#   any non-localhost base → Gradio transport (fresh queue job per submission):
#   POST {base}/gradio_api/upload → POST {base}/gradio_api/call/predict
#   → GET {base}/gradio_api/call/predict/{event_id} (SSE)
# Override auto-detect if needed: VITE_API_TRANSPORT=gradio | fastapi
# Backward compat: VITE_API_BASE (old Azure name) still works if VITE_API_BASE_URL not set
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
# VITE_API_TRANSPORT=fastapi
# For new HF Space production, set in Vercel Project → Settings → Environment Variables:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://YOUR_HF_USERNAME-satquery-backend.hf.space
# (public host only — selects the Gradio transport + direct fetched-image previews;
#  the /gradio_api queue calls themselves go through the same-origin proxy below)

# --- Vercel serverless proxy (SERVER-SIDE ONLY — never VITE_*, never in browser JS) ---
# Browser calls same-origin /api/gradio/*; frontend/api/gradio/[...path].ts forwards
# to the Space's /gradio_api/* with `Authorization: Bearer $HF_TOKEN` so ZeroGPU
# bills the account's own quota instead of the anonymous pool (which 429s).
# Set these in Vercel Project → Settings → Environment Variables (all environments):
# SATQUERY_SPACE_URL=https://YOUR_HF_USERNAME-satquery-backend.hf.space
# HF_TOKEN=hf_...  (HF account token with access to the Space — placeholder only, real value stays out of git)
# Local dev note: `vite dev` has no /api/gradio function, so localhost always calls
# the Space directly (anonymous quota) even with Gradio transport forced.
